---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StatCard from "../components/StatCard.astro";
import TeamGrid from "../components/TeamGrid.astro";
import { team } from "../data/team";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Active Bengaluru Foundation"
  description="ABF was born from neighbours showing up — a tight-knit group of COVID-era volunteers (Mercy Mission, ERT, Mercy Angels) who formalised in 2024 as a Section 8 NGO with 12A and 80G certifications."
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="bg-brand-yellow">
    <div class="container-x py-14 sm:py-20 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_1fr] items-center">
      <div>
        <span class="chip-red">About Us</span>
        <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-[1.65rem] sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl leading-[1.1] tracking-tight [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
          We didn't start as an NGO. <span class="accent-red">We started as neighbours.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg sm:text-xl text-brand-ink/80 leading-snug">
          Active Bengaluru Foundation was not born in a boardroom. It was born in the middle of a crisis — when a city was struggling to breathe, and a group of ordinary people decided they could not stand by and do nothing.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-3xl overflow-hidden shadow-card-lg ring-1 ring-brand-ink/10 bg-white">
        <img src="/images/about-hero.jpg" alt="About ABF" class="w-full" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ORIGIN — long-form prose -->
  <section class="container-narrow py-16 sm:py-20">
    <span class="chip">Origin</span>
    <h2 class="heading-section mt-3">The work that became ABF.</h2>
    <div class="prose-abf mt-6">
      <p>
        Long before we had a name, a registration, or a letterhead, the people behind ABF were already on the ground. Some of us were running community kitchens. Some were driving patients to hospitals at 2 AM. Some were tracking down oxygen cylinders when they had become near impossible to find.
      </p>
      <p>
        When COVID-19 hit Bengaluru, what had been scattered individual effort became something much larger. We came together under initiatives like <strong>Mercy Mission</strong> and co-founded the <strong>Emergency Response Team (ERT)</strong> — a volunteer-led effort that at its peak was helping families:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Find and book hospital beds in an overwhelmed system</li>
        <li>Arrange ambulances when none were available</li>
        <li>Source oxygen cylinders during the acute shortage</li>
        <li>Procure medicines and emergency supplies</li>
        <li>Navigate a healthcare system that was under enormous strain</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When patients did not survive, our team was also part of <strong>Mercy Angels</strong> — a group that quietly stepped in to support COVID burials and cremations, standing beside families in their most devastating moments.
      </p>
      <p>
        None of us planned for any of this. We simply <strong>showed up</strong> — and kept showing up.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY WE BECAME ABF -->
  <section class="bg-brand-cream">
    <div class="container-narrow py-16 sm:py-20">
      <span class="chip-red">Why we registered</span>
      <h2 class="heading-section mt-3">Why we became an NGO.</h2>
      <div class="prose-abf mt-6">
        <p>
          After COVID, the team stayed together. The need did not go away when the headlines did.
        </p>
        <p>
          But we realised something: goodwill and effort alone are not enough to create lasting change. To truly serve the community — to scale, to be accountable, to build trust with the people we work with — we needed structure.
        </p>
        <p>
          In <strong>2024</strong>, we formally registered <strong>Active Bengaluru Foundation</strong> as a Section 8 NGO, recognised under <strong>80G</strong> for tax-exempt donations. Not because the paperwork mattered to us, but because the people we serve deserved an organisation that would still be here five years from now — with proper processes, documented impact, and full accountability.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are still the same people. We just formalised the promise.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE PEOPLE BEHIND ABF — Team grids -->
  <section class="container-x py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="container-narrow px-0">
      <span class="chip">Our Core Team</span>
      <h2 class="heading-section mt-3">The people behind ABF.</h2>
      <p class="prose-abf mt-4">
        ABF is built by people who choose, every week, to give time to it — most of them with full-time careers, families, and other commitments. The team below is the spine of everything we do.
      </p>
    </div>

    {team.map((group) => (
      <TeamGrid group={group} />
    ))}
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT WE BELIEVE -->
  <section class="bg-brand-cream">
    <div class="container-narrow py-16 sm:py-20">
      <span class="chip">What we believe</span>
      <h2 class="heading-section mt-3">Be the bridge. <span class="accent-red">Don't duplicate.</span></h2>
      <div class="prose-abf mt-6">
        <p>
          We are not here to duplicate what others are already doing well. We are here to be the bridge — between the people who need help and the organisations, government systems, and resources that can provide it.
        </p>
        <p>
          We believe that <strong>community care is not charity. It is responsibility.</strong> And responsibility does not need a reason or a season.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- JOIN US -->
  <section class="bg-brand-yellow">
    <div class="container-narrow py-12 sm:py-16">
      <span class="chip-red">Join us</span>
      <h2 class="heading-section mt-3">Be part of the next thing we build.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-brand-ink/80 leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        ABF is always growing — in the work we do and in the people who do it with us. If you want to be part of something that genuinely makes a difference in Bengaluru, we would love to hear from you.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/get-involved" class="btn-primary">Get involved →</a>
        <a href="/donate" class="btn-call">Donate</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-secondary">Contact us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LEGAL / ACCOUNTABILITY -->
  <section class="bg-brand-ink text-white/85">
    <div class="container-x py-12 sm:py-16">
      <span class="chip bg-white/10 text-white">Legal &amp; registration</span>
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl mt-3 text-white">Built to be accountable.</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <StatCard value="2024" label="Registered (Section 8)" accent="yellow" />
        <StatCard value="12A" label="Income-tax exemption" accent="yellow" />
        <StatCard value="80G" label="Donation certification" accent="yellow" />
        <StatCard value="ABF" label="Bengaluru, Karnataka" accent="yellow" />
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-white/70 font-mono">CIN: U85500KA2024NPL184982</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
